{
  "video": {
    "id": "OK7_ReXhVaQ",
    "title": "Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OK7_ReXhVaQ",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 515,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 130,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.82,
      "end": 8.31,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "PROFESSOR ROBERT DORKIN:Hi, and welcome to a help session"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.31,
      "end": 9.85,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "on recombinant DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 9.85,
      "end": 12.25,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "Today we will be talking about the polymerase chain reaction"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.25,
      "end": 14.73,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "as well as DNA sequencing."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.73,
      "end": 17.17,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "The polymerase chain reaction, also known as"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 17.17,
      "end": 19.91,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "PCR, has many uses."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 19.91,
      "end": 22.34,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "One of the most common uses is to amplify a"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 22.34,
      "end": 25.18,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "desired section of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 25.18,
      "end": 28.53,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "What you need for the reaction is your DNA sequence of"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 28.53,
      "end": 36.16,
      "duration": 7.63,
      "text": "interest, DNA polymerase, DNA primers, and then four"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 36.16,
      "end": 37.41,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "different nucleotides."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 39.35,
      "end": 41.7,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "You combine all these together, and the first thing"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 41.7,
      "end": 43.95,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "that you do is you heat the reaction up."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 43.95,
      "end": 48.67,
      "duration": 4.72,
      "text": "What this does is that by adding heat to the system, you"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 48.67,
      "end": 51.41,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "break the hydrogen bonds between the two"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 51.41,
      "end": 53.9,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "different DNA strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 53.9,
      "end": 57.07,
      "duration": 3.17,
      "text": "This results in two separate DNA sequences."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 59.69,
      "end": 63.43,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "text": "Now what happens is that you allow the system to cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 63.43,
      "end": 68.03,
      "duration": 4.6,
      "text": "As it cools, the DNA primers are able to hybridize to this"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 68.03,
      "end": 70.4,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "separate strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 70.4,
      "end": 72.64,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "Now as you remember from lecture, when you're"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 72.64,
      "end": 76.03,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "synthesizing DNA, you synthesize from the five prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 76.03,
      "end": 78.61,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "to three prime direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 78.61,
      "end": 82.55,
      "duration": 3.94,
      "text": "This means that the primers you design have to match the"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 82.55,
      "end": 86.48,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "three prime end of your sequences of interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 86.48,
      "end": 90.14,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "So for example, if we were designing primers for these"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 90.14,
      "end": 103.4,
      "duration": 13.26,
      "text": "two sequences, one of them would be GGTA and the other"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 103.4,
      "end": 105.06,
      "duration": 1.66,
      "text": "one would be AGCT."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 116.09,
      "end": 119.46,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "Now, I've written four here."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 119.46,
      "end": 122.44,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "In actuality, these primers are generally longer, around"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 122.44,
      "end": 125.07,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "16 or so, 16 to 27."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 125.07,
      "end": 128.3,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "However, they can be a whole different variety of lengths"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 128.3,
      "end": 131.79,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "dependent on numerous different factors."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 131.79,
      "end": 134.51,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "The next thing that happens is that the DNA polymerase is"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 134.51,
      "end": 139.57,
      "duration": 5.06,
      "text": "going to bind to the DNA sequence with the primer."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 139.57,
      "end": 142.83,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "Once the DNA polymerase is bound, it's going to take some"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 142.83,
      "end": 146.8,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "of the free nucleotides in the surrounding area and slowly"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 146.8,
      "end": 148.8,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "add them to finish up the strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 156.77,
      "end": 160.14,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "And so on and so forth."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 160.14,
      "end": 163.99,
      "duration": 3.85,
      "text": "Once it's completed, we are going to have now doubled our"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 163.99,
      "end": 166.04,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "original DNA sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 166.04,
      "end": 167.97,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "We're going to have two strands that are identical to"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 167.97,
      "end": 170.02,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "the first one."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 170.02,
      "end": 173.58,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "As you can see, by repeating the steps, heating it,"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 173.58,
      "end": 177.16,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "allowing it to cool, allowing more primers to bond, and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 177.16,
      "end": 181.05,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "allowing the DNA polymerase to elongate, we can double the"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 181.05,
      "end": 183.15,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "number of sequences every round."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 183.15,
      "end": 185.69,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "And you can rapidly get a large amount"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 185.69,
      "end": 188.58,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "of the desired sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 188.58,
      "end": 191.95,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "PCR has other uses though besides simply increasing the"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 191.95,
      "end": 194.08,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "total amount of DNA that you have."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 194.08,
      "end": 198.32,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "One of the uses of PCR is to sequence DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 198.32,
      "end": 206.35,
      "duration": 8.03,
      "text": "Now, if we look over here, normally DNA is form of"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 206.35,
      "end": 209.92,
      "duration": 3.57,
      "text": "deoxyribonucleic acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 209.92,
      "end": 211.7,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "You have the phosphate group on the five prime end."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 215.08,
      "end": 217.325,
      "duration": 2.245,
      "text": "You have a hydroxyl group on the three prime end."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 220.84,
      "end": 223.59,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "This hydroxyl group is very important."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 223.59,
      "end": 227.06,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "That's because when a new nucleotide is added, this"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 227.06,
      "end": 231.39,
      "duration": 4.33,
      "text": "hydroxyl group undergoes a covalent bond with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 231.39,
      "end": 237.39,
      "duration": 6.0,
      "text": "phosphate on the new nucleotide and then adds a new"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 237.39,
      "end": 239.37,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "nucleotide that way."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 239.37,
      "end": 241.01,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "So you can see you're adding the five prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 241.01,
      "end": 243.2,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "the three prime direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 243.2,
      "end": 245.77,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "However, it is possible to create a"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 245.77,
      "end": 249.22,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "dideoxyribonucleic acid."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 249.22,
      "end": 252.98,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "The dideoxyribonucleic acid, instead of having a three"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 252.98,
      "end": 255.57,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "prime hydroxyl group, has a three prime hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 258.76,
      "end": 262.41,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "This three prime hydrogen is no longer capable of forming a"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 262.41,
      "end": 265.0,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "covalent bond with a phosphate."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 265.0,
      "end": 269.17,
      "duration": 4.17,
      "text": "That means as soon as the dideoxyribonucleic acid is"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 269.17,
      "end": 272.82,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "added to DNA, no further nucleotides can be added in"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 272.82,
      "end": 275.01,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "the series."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 275.01,
      "end": 278.67,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "Let's go back to our example with the primers."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 278.67,
      "end": 280.96,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "What does that mean for here?"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 280.96,
      "end": 285.25,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "Well, let's say you have a normal PCR reaction, but in"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 285.25,
      "end": 289.07,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "addition to the four deoxyribonucleic acids you"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 289.07,
      "end": 293.49,
      "duration": 4.42,
      "text": "have, you also take a little bit of dideoxyribonucleic"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 293.49,
      "end": 295.31,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "acids of one of the types."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 295.31,
      "end": 299.4,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "So let's say we add in some ddTTP."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 307.51,
      "end": 312.41,
      "duration": 4.9,
      "text": "Now what happens is that your DNA polymerase will go along"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 312.41,
      "end": 315.73,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "adding nucleotides as normal, but if it ever adds a"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 315.73,
      "end": 321.66,
      "duration": 5.93,
      "text": "dideoxyribonucleic acid, the polymerase will stop."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 321.66,
      "end": 325.92,
      "duration": 4.26,
      "text": "So if it adds, say a normal T here--"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 325.92,
      "end": 328.605,
      "duration": 2.685,
      "text": "continues down, continues down."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 331.16,
      "end": 334.74,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "If it adds a dideoxyribonucleic acid here,"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 334.74,
      "end": 336.51,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "it's going to stop, and we're going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 336.51,
      "end": 339.36,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "get a truncated sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 339.36,
      "end": 343.08,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "And so you can see that at any position that we have an A,"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 343.08,
      "end": 347.04,
      "duration": 3.96,
      "text": "it's going to be possible to have a truncated sequence of"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 347.04,
      "end": 348.81,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "that length."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 348.81,
      "end": 352.28,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "What this means that we're now going to, once the PCR is"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 352.28,
      "end": 357.36,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "text": "complete, have different DNA sequences of numerous"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 357.36,
      "end": 360.18,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "different lengths."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 360.18,
      "end": 362.98,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "But the one thing they're all going to have in common is"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 362.98,
      "end": 369.35,
      "duration": 6.37,
      "text": "that they're all going to end with a T. So you can imagine"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 369.35,
      "end": 373.09,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "text": "doing this now for each of the four different letters."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 373.09,
      "end": 376.03,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "Then we can take them and run them out of a gel."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 376.03,
      "end": 377.61,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "Let's go look at such a gel over here."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 382.27,
      "end": 385.02,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "Here we have a gel."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 385.02,
      "end": 387.88,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "Each of these letters represents which"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 387.88,
      "end": 392.53,
      "duration": 4.65,
      "text": "dideoxyribonucleic acid was used for that experiment."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 392.53,
      "end": 397.33,
      "duration": 4.8,
      "text": "And then the PCR was run out on the gel."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 397.33,
      "end": 401.4,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "As you remember, the strands close to the bottom are the"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 401.4,
      "end": 404.31,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "shorter strands, and the strands close to the top are"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 404.31,
      "end": 407.4,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "the longer strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 407.4,
      "end": 413.26,
      "duration": 5.86,
      "text": "So if we look at this gel, we know that the shortest strand"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 413.26,
      "end": 428.931,
      "duration": 15.671,
      "text": "ends with a G. The next shortest strand ends in a T."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 428.931,
      "end": 431.02,
      "duration": 2.089,
      "text": "Oh, sorry, ends in an A, excuse me."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 434.5,
      "end": 444.13,
      "duration": 9.63,
      "text": "Then the next short strand ends in a T, then two A's,"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 444.13,
      "end": 451.41,
      "duration": 7.28,
      "text": "then a G, then a C, then a T. So as you can see, this is one"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 451.41,
      "end": 455.49,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "way to determine the sequence of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 455.49,
      "end": 459.57,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "Another way has been devised, which is even faster."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 459.57,
      "end": 463.0,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "Instead of running the sequences all out in different"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 463.0,
      "end": 467.38,
      "duration": 4.38,
      "text": "polymerase chain reactions, what they do is they have some"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 467.38,
      "end": 470.84,
      "duration": 3.46,
      "text": "of each of the dideoxynucleotides together."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 470.84,
      "end": 474.82,
      "duration": 3.98,
      "text": "But now, they fluorescently label them, such that you have"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 474.82,
      "end": 476.64,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "a different fluorescent label on each"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 476.64,
      "end": 479.29,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "dideoxyribonucleic acid."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 479.29,
      "end": 481.84,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "Now what happens is that you can run it"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 481.84,
      "end": 483.87,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "out all on one column."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 483.87,
      "end": 487.11,
      "duration": 3.24,
      "text": "And then by just looking at the colors, you can determine"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 487.11,
      "end": 488.51,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "what the sequence is."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 488.51,
      "end": 490.976,
      "duration": 2.466,
      "text": "So once again, the sequence would be GATAAGCT."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 497.88,
      "end": 500.75,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "And so this way, you can more efficiently, more rapidly,"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 500.75,
      "end": 503.57,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "determine what the DNA sequence is."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 503.57,
      "end": 507.41,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "This has been two examples of polymerase chain reactions and"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 507.41,
      "end": 508.51,
      "duration": 1.1,
      "text": "their uses."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 508.51,
